course: dictionary
lesson: 6387
title: What multiplication means
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Multiplication is a quick way of adding the same number again and again. 3 × 4 means three groups of four, which is 4 + 4 + 4 = 12. The sign × shows multiplication.
explain: In the Alice story, the Mock Turtle's school has «Ambition, Distraction, Uglification and Derision» for four kinds of sums. Alice's word «beautify» means to make something prettier, so «uglify» must mean the opposite. Clue words help you see what a new word is about.
explain: Multiplication can also mean a big increase in number, as with germs. In science, «the multiplication of bacteria» means the bacteria are growing in number very quickly. The meaning is the same: many more of something, fast.
explain: Check your answer by swapping in the meaning. If 3 × 4 means three groups of four, then 4 + 4 + 4 should give the same answer as 3 × 4. If it does, you are right.
fact: Multiplication is the operation shown by the sign ×.
fact: 3 × 4 means three groups of four, which is 12.
fact: Multiplication comes before addition, so 2 + 3 × 4 = 14, because 3 × 4 = 12 and then 2 + 12 = 14.
fact: Times tables are lists of multiplication facts, such as 5 × 6 = 30.
fact: In science, the multiplication of bacteria or cells means they grow in number very quickly.
exercise: What does 3 × 4 mean? | Four take away three, which makes 1 | Twelve groups of nothing | Three plus four, which makes 7 | *Three groups of four, which makes 12
exercise: The Mock Turtle's school has «Ambition, Distraction, Uglification and Derision» for four kinds of sums. Which one is multiplication? | Derision | Ambition | *Uglification | Distraction
exercise: In «2 + 3 × 4 = 14», which sum is worked out first? | Addition, 2 + 3 | It does not matter which one comes first | Both at the same time | *Multiplication, 3 × 4
test: What does 5 × 2 mean? | Five take away two, which makes 3 | Five plus two, which makes 7 | *Five groups of two, which makes 10 | Two groups of nothing
test: Which word describes bacteria growing in number very quickly? | Division | *Multiplication | Subtraction | Addition
exam: What is 4 × 3? | 43 | 1 | *12 | 7
